# Frontend conventions (Tauri + SvelteKit)

## Stack

Svelte 5 (Runes), SvelteKit (`src/routes`), TypeScript, Tailwind v4 (`@import "tailwindcss"` in `src/app.css`), Tauri API (`@tauri-apps/api`), **[Bits UI](https://bits-ui.com/)** (`bits-ui`) for headless UI primitives. Do not use Svelte 4-style patterns (`export let`) in new code.

## Generic UI primitives (Bits UI)

Use **[Bits UI](https://bits-ui.com/)** (`bits-ui`) for reusable, accessible primitives: dialogs, select, dropdowns, tabs, tooltips, and similar patterns.

- Prefer **Bits UI + Tailwind** instead of hand-rolled focus traps, ARIA, and keyboard handling for those cases.
- Plain `<input>` / `<textarea>` or app-specific layout are fine when a Bits primitive does not apply or adds no benefit.

## Naming and layout

- Use **kebab-case** for directories and filenames (no PascalCase filenames).
- **Reusable UI**: `src/lib/components/<kebab-name>/`.
- **Routes**: follow SvelteKit conventions under `src/routes/`.

## One component set (same directory)

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `index.ts` | `export { default as … } from "./….svelte"` |
| `<name>.svelte` | Implementation |
| `<name>.stories.ts` | Storybook (CSF) |
| `<name>.spec.ts` | Vitest + Testing Library |

Prefer exposing components via `$lib/components/<dir>`.

## Style and quality

- **Imports**: `simple-import-sort` (`pnpm lint:fix`).
- **Functions**: aim for **≤ ~100 lines** (split when they grow longer).
- **Line endings**: **LF** (per `.editorconfig`).
- **Styling**: prefer Tailwind. Avoid huge `<style>` blocks.

## Tests and Storybook

- **spec**: use `vi.mock` so Tauri and similar can be swapped. Do not break Vitest resolution conditions in `vite.config.ts`.
- **stories**: `Meta` / `StoryObj` from `@storybook/sveltekit`. When the browser has no Tauri, follow existing DEV fallbacks / mocking patterns.

## For agents

Change only the files needed for the request. For new UI, align with the **four-file layout** above when practical.
